  "scope": [
    "Classify privacy-safe control-package reads from supported sanitized Codex App Server action shapes without retaining raw commands or output.",
    "Make cache sensitivity and cache-control validity first-class in deterministic comparison analysis, so routing or model claims fail closed when cache imbalance can dominate the result.",
    "Retain a reusable, versioned evaluation method and protocol template for later Temple workflow changes and newly released models without authorizing a live Provider run."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Sanitized regression fixtures recognize supported control reads, preserve unsafe or ambiguous reads as unknown, and retain no raw command or output content.",
    "Reports expose gross input, cached input, non-cached input, output, Operational Tokens, cache share, repetition spread, and an explicit cache-control validity result; causal efficiency claims remain blocked when validity is insufficient.",
    "A human-facing guide and copyable protocol template define hypotheses, factors, counterbalancing, cache strategy, quality gates, budgets, stop conditions, privacy, approval, and reporting for process and model comparisons.",
    "WI-0141 retained artifacts remain byte-identical and this Work Item performs no model generation, external write, release, or publication."
  ],
